WEBVTT

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:08.200
Bone of anchovy...

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.280
Leaf of radish...

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.470
Ancient onion...

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:16.860
And the secret ingredient,
a massive amount of hot peppers...

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:21.230
The dough for the Nonoha Sweets:
Death Special is complete.

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.250
That's intense!

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.790
With a shock like this...

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:34.540
He's always gone back to normal
with a single cookie, but...

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:40.500
Even though I made him eat
all the sweets last time,

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:43.450
Kaito wouldn't go back to his old self.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:47.260
It's like Kaito is...

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:51.190
More and more, he's becoming
someone I don't know.

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:04.650
I'm the only one who can
cheer Kaito up, right?!

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:09.790
He can't keep moping around.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:13.710
Kaito, I've made the ultimate sweets!

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:15.010
Be my guinea pig...

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:17.170
I mean, give them a taste!

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:18.890
The door's open, right?

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:20.050
I'm coming in.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:22.470
Um...

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.010
What do you need with Mr. Kaito?

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:29.320
Who are you?!

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:50.920
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.710
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:55.500
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:58.260
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:02.760
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:07.470
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:09.680
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:12.350
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:14.360
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:16.650
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.610
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:21.400
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:25.950
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.200
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:32.870
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:35.130
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:37.460
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:40.090
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:45.970
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:51.640
Brain diver

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:56.440
Brain diver

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:05.030
The Proof of Betrayal

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:10.140
You're Gammon's younger sister?!

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:12.170
I'm Miharu Sakanoue.

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:13.600
Thank you for looking after Bro...

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:15.670
I mean, my big brother!

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:17.900
Unbelievable, ain't it?

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:20.210
How could he have a sister like this?

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:21.540
I hear that a lot.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:24.680
Still, it's not as if
he gave birth to me.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:31.560
I'm sorry, I haven't
eaten since last night.

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:38.230
It's so delicious!

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:39.250
No way!

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:40.820
You're right, it's great!

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:44.730
My skill at this kind of cooking

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:47.300
got in the way of my scheme, huh?

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:48.370
"Scheme"?

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:50.500
Say, shall I teach you the recipe?

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:52.040
I think you'll be shocked!

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:55.650
Um, not, I'm really no good at cooking.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:58.540
My brother always cooks for us.

00:03:58.930 --> 00:03:59.880
For real?!

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:01.880
With a face like that?!

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:06.140
It's not as if people
cook with their faces.

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:11.140
I guess we didn't know much about Gammon.

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:13.810
I never thought he'd
have a sister like this,

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:16.570
or do things around the house.

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:19.410
Still, it's worrisome.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:21.990
Gammon never came home last night, right?

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:26.490
Oh, it's not unusual for
him to not come home,

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:29.890
but he's always sure to let me know.

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:32.790
And this morning, this was in the mail,

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:34.410
from my brother to me.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.380
What is this?

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:39.850
It's a check.

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:41.790
A check?! I've never seen one!

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:43.740
Look at all these zeroes!

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:46.270
One, ten, a hundred, a
thousand, ten thousand...

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:49.760
I've lost my appetite!

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:53.300
Was there anything different
about him yesterday?

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:54.640
My brother?

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:57.240
If you know something, please tell me.

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:58.460
Where he may have gone...

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:18.130
Well, well!

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:21.210
What a handsome guest we have.

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:23.780
Let Gammon in, 'kay?
Thanks!
ERENA

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:24.090
This is my introduction,
from Erena Himekawa.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.840
I wanna meet Rook Banjo Crossfield.

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:31.640
Why would Master Rook
meet some pissant Solver?

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:35.600
What kinda trickery did you use
to get through security?

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:37.490
It's a legit offer. Move.

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:38.390
Huh?

00:05:38.390 --> 00:05:39.370
I'll crush you.

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:40.660
Try it.

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:45.090
I ain't a Solver today!

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:47.530
I came here as a Giver,
same as you pricks.

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:50.960
You really think you
can beat me as a Giver?

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:52.540
You stupid children!

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:55.160
I guess it can't be helped.

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:56.970
Care to have a little fun?

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:00.720
Our parents are gone.

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:06.040
My brother is the one who's
raised me this whole time.

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:09.780
He's loved making puzzles
since we were children.

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:13.150
When his talent was discovered,
he became a puzzle maker

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:16.810
and raised me and gave
me everything I wanted.

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:22.130
But before we knew it,
he was making puzzles just for money.

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:24.860
And then his face got all gloomy...

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:30.950
But recently, he's started smiling again!

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:32.450
"Kaito sucks!"

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:36.500
"I can't stand Kaito!"
he'd say, all animated.

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:40.740
And then in his sleep, he'd
be all "Nonoha! Nonoha!"

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:42.140
Huh? Me?

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:45.290
That's why I thought maybe
you two knew something.

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:49.800
Sorry, if we learn something,
we'll let you know right away.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:51.270
Thank you.

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:54.150
Well, I'll get by on
convenience-store lunches

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:56.060
till my brother gets back!

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:02.270
Where the did Gammon run off to?

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:05.790
I wonder if something happened
after he challenged you?

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:07.370
Dunno.

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:09.130
You're not even worried?

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:11.540
Whatever happens is on his head.

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:13.250
Don't be like that!

00:07:23.780 --> 00:07:25.500
Hey, Kaito!

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:28.290
What is it?

00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:31.090
Uh, nothin'.

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:46.400
This is my puzzle:

00:07:46.830 --> 00:07:49.180
Use the dice to fill in the squares.

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:51.620
However, none of the
dice's faces can match,

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:54.180
either vertically or horizontally.

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:56.920
The same goes for the
areas blocked off in red.

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:59.240
You can't have any matching faces.

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:01.470
What do you think? Simple or difficult?

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:03.730
A most beautiful creation, isn't it?!

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:10.030
Hey, don't do that!

00:08:10.030 --> 00:08:10.810
My puzzle is-

00:08:10.810 --> 00:08:12.150
He set it up.
My puzzle is-

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:13.250
What?!

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:17.550
What's more, it's in
the most difficult way!

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:21.280
You're quite good.

00:08:21.280 --> 00:08:23.150
This is enough to impress you?

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:27.650
I guess I know what the
POG's level is now.

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:42.830
H..He solved it.

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:46.410
The dice's faces don't
match even on the sides!

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:48.070
For all four sides!

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:54.360
I'll be goin' now.

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:00.930
Wait there.

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:02.680
This time, you face me!

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:08.020
What the hell is this?

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:12.050
Try making your way to the goal.

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:15.510
If you, do the path will
spell out a wonderful name.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:21.920
M-A-Z-E, Maze.

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:23.910
Could that be your name?

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:31.390
But if you do like this...

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:34.270
Just what are you doing?

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:43.360
"Amazed"!

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:46.160
Like it says, you're amazed, aren't ya?

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:47.640
I'm next!

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:48.710
That's enough.
I'm next!

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:56.200
I am your next opponent.

00:09:56.820 --> 00:09:58.410
Mr. Bishop!

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:01.030
And here's the mid-level boss?

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:07.320
Miharu sure was cute, huh?

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:09.670
If I hadn't gone by your room...

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:11.600
Could it be...

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:12.570
You're an idiot.

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:14.080
Wait!

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:18.180
Nonoha-poo! Kaito-poo!

00:10:21.710 --> 00:10:23.360
It's been a while-poo!

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:34.130
My apologies for the wait.

00:10:34.990 --> 00:10:36.030
Please, this way.

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:42.240
Hey, Mr. Bishop!

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:44.310
What happened to my bike?

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:47.130
We gave it a few upgrades.

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:48.150
What?!

00:10:48.150 --> 00:10:49.850
Not to worry.

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:51.540
It will have no problems running.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:54.750
We've prepared a great stage,

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:56.600
one where victory will be plain to see.

00:10:56.600 --> 00:10:58.770
You won't be tryin' no
underhanded tricks, right?

00:10:58.770 --> 00:10:59.800
Of course not.

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:04.450
This is an Iron Horse
Dogfight, where bikers

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:07.780
seek to destroy the rider behind them.

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:10.980
And this is the circuit we'll be racing.

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:13.310
That's my...

00:11:13.350 --> 00:11:16.800
That is where you'll start the race.

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:19.800
Allow me to explain the rules.

00:11:21.590 --> 00:11:24.100
This is a map of the full circuit.

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:27.290
The course is divided into five lanes.

00:11:27.690 --> 00:11:31.910
It's made so that both our bikes
will maintain a set speed,

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:33.570
so to catch up to each other,

00:11:33.570 --> 00:11:36.450
we'll have to use the lane-change points.

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:38.790
Activating these will let you

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:41.540
move to the neighboring lane.

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:43.380
By the same token,

00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:46.640
you can also forcibly
change your opponent's route.

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:50.200
However, you can't freely return to

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:52.560
a point that you've activated.

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:55.590
You can control a maximum of ten points

00:11:55.590 --> 00:11:57.190
throughout the course.

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:00.780
Activating an eleventh point

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:04.580
will cause the first point
to return to its original position.

00:12:06.710 --> 00:12:08.700
No matter which one of us activates it?

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:11.790
Correct, we have ten points
between the two of us.

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:15.100
My bike is of the same height,

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:18.120
and fitted with a light
gun and tail sensor.

00:12:18.740 --> 00:12:21.930
If either of us come up from behind

00:12:21.930 --> 00:12:25.430
and shine the flashlight
on the other's sensor...

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:26.920
It's the end.

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:29.560
The end?

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:33.060
The bikes are fitted with explosives.

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:34.340
Fine with me.

00:12:34.340 --> 00:12:36.740
This will settle things loud and clear.

00:12:39.680 --> 00:12:41.840
Activate the lane-change points

00:12:41.840 --> 00:12:46.070
by entering the numbers on
the left-side controller.

00:12:46.730 --> 00:12:48.330
Are you ready?

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:50.560
Yeah, whenever you are.

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:53.870
Please let me ask one thing.

00:12:54.770 --> 00:12:57.370
Why did you accept Master
Rook's invitation?

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:00.180
For proof.

00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:01.440
Proof?

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:05.240
Proof that I'm better than Kaito Daimon.

00:13:05.780 --> 00:13:07.840
I'll become a POG Giver

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:09.390
and crush that bastard!

00:13:13.540 --> 00:13:15.830
I'm afraid we can't have that.

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:20.950
He is absolutely essential
for what we have in mind.

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:22.990
I'll take his place.

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:25.280
You're saying you possess such skill?

00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:32.100
That's why your boss called me, right?

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:33.380
I see.

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:36.710
However, I am not as wise as Master Rook.

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:42.460
I cannot acknowledge that skill
until I've tested it for myself.

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:45.720
Then, I'll show ya right now!

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:01.280
Gammon's with the POG?

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:03.730
Is that true, Erena?

00:14:03.770 --> 00:14:08.010
What could I possibly
gain from lying to you?

00:14:08.010 --> 00:14:09.900
What the hell's going on?

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:11.740
Master Rook gave him an offer.

00:14:12.050 --> 00:14:13.030
Rook did?!

00:14:13.030 --> 00:14:16.990
Yes, and it was Galileo
himself who accepted.

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:19.290
I get it.

00:14:19.850 --> 00:14:22.120
That puzzle he prepared last night...

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:24.320
I thought it was kinda grandiose.

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:26.690
Why are you telling us this?

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:28.800
Well...

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:32.220
Let's say, a lot has changed
since the last time we met.

00:14:32.710 --> 00:14:34.810
I used to like him, but...

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:36.390
Huh? What was that?

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:39.740
L..Look, I've told you, all right?

00:14:39.740 --> 00:14:44.060
You can bring him back or
reform him or whatever.

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:45.350
You're his "friends"?

00:14:45.350 --> 00:14:47.770
You're not in grade school
anymore, you idiots.

00:14:47.770 --> 00:14:49.280
I could care less.

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:50.280
Kaito!

00:14:51.210 --> 00:14:53.450
If he wants to go to the POG or wherever,

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:54.860
his ass can go.

00:14:54.860 --> 00:14:56.910
I got no reason to stop him.

00:15:03.350 --> 00:15:07.770
I just gotta catch up
and flash the light-gun.

00:15:07.770 --> 00:15:09.530
So, of course, I gotta stay on him.

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:13.080
If we're both at the same, set speed,

00:15:13.080 --> 00:15:15.490
the key to winning will
be drivin' him out

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:17.600
to where the circuit's route is longest.

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:19.560
That's where this thing comes in!

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:27.190
It's begun.

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:31.200
And I'm headed for where the
circuit route is shortest!

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:36.870
He put me on the outside!

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:45.070
And he gets the inside lane?

00:15:45.070 --> 00:15:46.680
I don't think so!

00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:47.880
Click, sucker!

00:15:52.710 --> 00:15:55.270
Okay, come on out!

00:15:56.530 --> 00:15:58.430
Thank you for bringing us here.

00:15:58.430 --> 00:16:00.540
I don't need your thanks.

00:16:00.540 --> 00:16:02.650
I was headed this way anyway.

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:05.600
So, what will you do after this?

00:16:05.600 --> 00:16:07.080
After this?

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:11.090
Well, Kaito and I are
gonna go grocery shopping.

00:16:11.090 --> 00:16:12.610
That's not what I meant.

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:18.700
I think it's about time you
separate from him, too.

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:21.420
Now you're saying that?

00:16:21.420 --> 00:16:22.750
You don't want to die, do you?

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:26.310
Hey, I think that's Erena!

00:16:26.310 --> 00:16:27.970
Yeah, it's Erena Himekawa!

00:16:27.970 --> 00:16:29.740
She's cuter than on TV!

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:29.740
Oh, Kaito!

00:16:29.740 --> 00:16:30.840
Everyone!

00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:33.400
Please look forward to my new single,

00:16:31.990 --> 00:16:33.400
Hey, Kaito! Wait!

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:36.680
"Solve the Puzzle of Love,"
releasing this month!

00:16:37.090 --> 00:16:38.720
Well, see you later, Erena.

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:39.580
Wait!

00:16:40.420 --> 00:16:41.220
Here.

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:46.220
Try not to get too much
in his way, all right?

00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:49.450
What are you doing? Hurry up and drive!

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:50.600
Bye-bye-poo!

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:52.190
Kaito!

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:56.910
He's changed somehow, too.

00:16:57.990 --> 00:16:59.710
Kaito!

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:03.260
Where the heck did he go?

00:17:03.260 --> 00:17:04.800
Kaito!

00:17:09.810 --> 00:17:14.040
Don't tell me he really
thought I got in the way.

00:17:14.950 --> 00:17:17.590
How cruel! Just you watch!

00:17:17.590 --> 00:17:18.880
When I put my mind to it,

00:17:18.880 --> 00:17:21.480
I can solve this puzzle and another, and...

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:25.620
I can't do it!

00:17:25.620 --> 00:17:27.480
Kaito!

00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:40.760
I'm sure you know this by now.

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:43.830
Kaito Daimon is a Phi-Brain child.

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:46.090
The principal told us.

00:17:46.090 --> 00:17:47.570
He said I'm one, too.

00:17:47.570 --> 00:17:49.920
I've got what it takes to be a Phi-Brain!

00:17:56.360 --> 00:17:58.500
That's just his opinion.

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:02.350
Proof of which is that you do not own
the Armlet of Orpheus.

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:05.180
Yeah, I didn't want that thing!

00:18:05.790 --> 00:18:07.900
When that thing possesses Kaito,

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:10.420
he's a goddamn unsightly disgrace!

00:18:10.420 --> 00:18:14.070
But in exchange, he has
gained tremendous power.

00:18:15.050 --> 00:18:17.590
Owning the Armlet of
Orpheus allows a person

00:18:17.590 --> 00:18:20.460
to approach Phi-Brain potential.

00:18:24.980 --> 00:18:26.510
Comin' in the next one, huh?!

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:39.730
Almost.

00:18:39.730 --> 00:18:41.300
That was an admirable escape.

00:18:42.150 --> 00:18:44.350
It's not just the routes he takes:

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:46.540
I also have to remember
which point will go back

00:18:46.540 --> 00:18:48.310
to its original position next.

00:18:49.300 --> 00:18:50.810
Like this, maybe?

00:18:51.620 --> 00:18:52.710
No...

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:54.580
Like this?

00:18:59.040 --> 00:19:01.360
Huh? I solved it.

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:04.040
It's the first time I've solved one.

00:19:06.110 --> 00:19:08.430
I solved a puzzle!

00:19:08.430 --> 00:19:09.950
Kaito!

00:19:11.180 --> 00:19:12.940
The Puzzle of God

00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:16.040
will lead humanity
to an elevated dimension.

00:19:16.040 --> 00:19:19.350
It is the ultimate doorway,
if you will, to supremacy.

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:22.480
Believing that the man on the street,

00:19:22.480 --> 00:19:24.050
that you by your own strength,

00:19:24.050 --> 00:19:25.370
would be able to solve it

00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:27.850
is the height of conceit, don't you think?

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:38.240
What's the matter?

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:41.220
You've been activating points
that are of no meaning.

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:43.820
Are you hoping for a lucky punch?

00:19:44.510 --> 00:19:45.900
It's no use.

00:19:45.900 --> 00:19:47.190
Without the Armlet of Orpheus,

00:19:47.190 --> 00:19:48.970
you could not hope for such a miraculous-

00:19:54.230 --> 00:19:57.060
You talk a lot of uppity BS,

00:19:57.060 --> 00:20:00.380
but the Armlet of Orpheus
really ain't all that, is it?!

00:20:01.210 --> 00:20:05.640
You still haven't seen what
a friggin' genius I am!

00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:14.480
Eat this!

00:20:17.800 --> 00:20:19.900
You thought that would
be enough to get me?

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:21.550
You're nothing but a...

00:20:27.090 --> 00:20:28.080
Oh, no!

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:32.540
Gotcha!

00:20:57.760 --> 00:20:59.080
I..It can't be...

00:20:59.080 --> 00:21:01.330
He laid his trap while doing those

00:21:01.330 --> 00:21:02.480
meaningless lane changes?

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:03.820
That's checkmate.

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:09.610
I won't let anyone get in my way.

00:21:09.610 --> 00:21:12.040
Even if God and fate
are stacked against me!

00:21:16.270 --> 00:21:17.780
I admit it.

00:21:18.440 --> 00:21:20.090
You've defeated me.

00:21:22.520 --> 00:21:25.550
No one can call me a bother after this.

00:21:28.430 --> 00:21:31.470
Hey, Kaito! I solved it, Kaito!

00:21:32.050 --> 00:21:34.390
Huh? Are you still not back?

00:21:34.390 --> 00:21:35.570
Kaito!

00:21:35.570 --> 00:21:37.300
You there? You not there?

00:21:37.300 --> 00:21:39.910
If you're not there,
say you're not there!

00:21:39.910 --> 00:21:41.700
Hey, Kaito!

00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:44.040
Hey! You there?

00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:47.850
Such a trifling wish as
"I want to beat Kaito"

00:21:47.850 --> 00:21:49.490
does not become you.

00:21:50.150 --> 00:21:51.580
What was that?!

00:21:52.130 --> 00:21:54.930
I'm saying that even without
the Armlet of Orpheus,

00:21:54.930 --> 00:21:59.010
I think that you can challenge
the Puzzle of God.

00:21:59.530 --> 00:22:00.420
What?

00:22:00.790 --> 00:22:03.020
You are worthy.

00:22:03.020 --> 00:22:04.570
Worthy to solve the Puzzle of God,

00:22:04.570 --> 00:22:06.220
to open the Book of God,

00:22:06.220 --> 00:22:08.930
to obtain absolute power.

00:22:09.560 --> 00:22:11.930
Absolute power...

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:15.140
Now then, come with me.

00:22:15.720 --> 00:22:17.740
But once you climb these stairs,

00:22:17.740 --> 00:22:20.090
there's no turning back.

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:41.540
Tsukue no ue de umareta sekai
A world born on top of a desk

00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:47.340
Ichiban saki ni kimi ni misetakatta
I wanted to show it to you first of all

00:22:47.770 --> 00:22:52.090
Karappo no heya sotto nukedashite
I sneaked silently out of that empty room

00:22:52.090 --> 00:22:57.210
Hashirihajimeteta
And started running

00:22:58.290 --> 00:23:02.610
Iki hazumasete oka o noboru to
Breathing heavily, I climbed the hill

00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:08.220
Kimi ga saki ni tsuite matte ita ne
And you were already there, waiting

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:13.160
Takusan no hajimete kimi to mitsuketa
There were so many treasures that I first

00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:17.910
Takaramono datta
Discovered with you

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:24.020
Kanashisa de afureta toki wa
That time when I was overcome with sadness

00:23:24.020 --> 00:23:26.600
Nanimo iwazu ni tada
You said nothing

00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:29.250
Soba ni ite kureta ne
Just stayed there by my side, didn't you?

00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:33.910
Imademo wasurenai yo
Even now, I haven't forgotten

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:39.180
Mata aou ne, yakusoku o shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:44.400
Kei wa shinai, ano hi no sayonara
It won't fade, the "goodbye" of that day

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:50.050
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I have, the path you gave me

00:23:50.050 --> 00:23:58.960
Zutto kokoro no naka hikaru yo
Will always shine within my heart

00:24:02.630 --> 00:24:06.710
Mr. Kaito, I think I'm going
to go look for my brother!

00:24:06.710 --> 00:24:09.470
"Go look"? You have an idea where he is?

00:24:09.470 --> 00:24:10.820
No, I don't.

00:24:10.820 --> 00:24:13.590
But if I try hard, I might find him.

00:24:13.720 --> 00:24:15.760
Wouldn't it be better just to wait?

00:24:15.760 --> 00:24:17.330
I can't do that!

00:24:17.330 --> 00:24:21.040
I've already used up the
check that he left me!

00:24:21.040 --> 00:24:23.740
Next time, "The Speeding Challenger"

00:24:21.460 --> 00:24:27.500
The Speeding Challenger

00:24:23.740 --> 00:24:26.320
What did you use all that money on?!
